{"compatibility":"as-is","safety_note_md":"# SafeStan Safety Note

Compatibility: as-is.

Protected data: `y`.

Generated files: `model_safe.stan`, `data_safe.json`.

No changes were required. The protected observation `y` is a top-level data variable and is scored exactly once with the built-in `binomial_logit` distribution using a plain sampling statement. Context data `N` and `K` are not protected. Each parameter (`mu`, `sigma`, and `alpha`) has exactly one built-in prior before later use.
","model_safe_stan":"data {
  int<lower=0> N; // items
  array[N] int<lower=0> K; // initial trials
  array[N] int<lower=0> y; // initial successes
}
parameters {
  real mu; // population mean of success log-odds
  real<lower=0> sigma; // population sd of success log-odds
  vector[N] alpha; // success log-odds
}
model {
  mu ~ normal(-1, 1); // hyperprior
  sigma ~ normal(0, 1); // hyperprior
  alpha ~ normal(mu, sigma); // prior (hierarchical)
  y ~ binomial_logit(K, alpha); // likelihood
}
generated quantities {
  vector[N] theta; // chance of success

  for (n in 1 : N) {
    theta[n] = inv_logit(alpha[n]);
  }
}

","data_safe_json":"{
  "K": [
    2,
    2,
    1,
    1
  ],
  "N": 4,
  "y": [
    1,
    2,
    1,
    1
  ]
}
","protected_variables":["y"]}
